/*
  AdvancedSettings.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 feature view · 0198 · AdvancedSettings (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. Every key the native `AdvancedSettings`
  resolves (table "AdvancedSettings") lives here with its web `t(key, default)` English value. These
  entries fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are kept
  in a per-surface table so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings without editing the
  shared catalog.

  The first block is extracted from the web source
  (features/settings/components/AdvancedSettings.tsx + lib/confirmSilence.ts). The web component uses
  the `settings` i18n namespace, so its keys read `advanced.restoreConfirms.*`; the silence-key labels
  come from `useSilenceKeyLabel` (`...keys.*`). The remainder backs the native state envelope (loading
  skeleton, empty title, error / retry chrome, the freshness chip, the connectivity banner) and the
  accessibility summaries — none of which exist as English literals in the Swift sources.
*/

/* --- Keys from the web source (parity) --- */
"advanced.restoreConfirms.title" = "Confirmation prompts";
"advanced.restoreConfirms.description" = "Re-enable “Don’t ask again” prompts you previously silenced.";
"advanced.restoreConfirms.restoreAll" = "Restore all";
"advanced.restoreConfirms.restore" = "Restore";
"advanced.restoreConfirms.empty" = "No silenced prompts. Tick “Don’t ask again” on a confirmation dialog to silence it.";

/* --- Friendly silence-key labels (web useSilenceKeyLabel) --- */
"advanced.restoreConfirms.keys.discardDraft" = "Discard unsaved draft";
"advanced.restoreConfirms.keys.unsavedNavigation" = "Leave page with unsaved changes";

/* --- Native state envelope (loading / empty title / error) --- */
